  * h-main (70B model): 100% recall (42/42 unique Pareto tuples) and 100% precision (81/81 configs truly Pareto-optimal) using 200 evaluations, well above the ≥90% target. All four structural regularities (TP dominance, cache equivalence, maxr plateau, SJF×concurrency interaction) transferred from the 14B model.
  * h-robustness (7B model): 100% recall (21/21 unique Pareto tuples) using 200 evaluations (11.9% of the 1,680 valid configs), far exceeding the ≥80% target. Dynamic TP validation correctly excluded tp=8 (NumHeads=28 not divisible by 8), confirming the algorithm handles invalid TP configurations gracefully.
  * Cross-model pattern: Pareto front complexity scales with model size — 21 unique tuples (7B), 35 (14B), 42 (70B) — and the search achieves 100% recall on all three. The structural regularities exploited by the search are properties of BLIS's simulation engine, not model-specific artifacts.
  * No surprises or regressions: 14B recall verified as still 35/35 = 100%. The 70B model showed steeper maxr sensitivity below 256 (14% rps loss vs 0% for 14B), but this did not create additional Pareto points because those configs are dominated on both rps and ttft.

